1
00:00:00,585 --> 00:00:04,795
(Howard:)So this spring, I get to go
to the International Space Station.

2
00:00:04,964 --> 00:00:08,504
(Mrs Cooper:)Oh, my word, a trip to the heavens.

3
00:00:10,011 --> 00:00:14,351
If you ever wanna live there eternally,
I've got a good book you could read.

4
00:00:15,308 --> 00:00:18,098
(Howard:)I watch the Charlie Brown
Christmas Special every year...

5
00:00:18,269 --> 00:00:19,309
(Howard:)...so I get the gist.

6
00:00:19,478 --> 00:00:21,648
(Mrs Cooper:)I bet your mom is really proud of you.

7
00:00:21,814 --> 00:00:26,154
(Howard:)Nope. She says if I don't back out,
she's gonna go on a hunger strike.

8
00:00:26,319 --> 00:00:30,619
Um, it would take years before she'd be
in any kind of danger, but still.

9
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:33,490
(Sheldon:)I've got a treat for us tomorrow, Mom.

10
00:00:33,659 --> 00:00:36,869
(Sheldon:)I'm taking you to see
Saul Perlmutter give a lecture...

11
00:00:37,038 --> 00:00:39,538
(Sheldon:)...about his Nobel Prize-winning
work in cosmology.

12
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:42,377
(Sheldon:)And the best part is,
at the Q and A afterward...

13
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:46,963
(Sheldon:)...I've worked up a couple of
Q's that will stump his sorry A.

14
00:00:48,758 --> 00:00:52,008
(Mrs Cooper:)I don't know, Shelly. I thought we could
do a little sightseeing.

15
00:00:52,178 --> 00:00:57,018
(Sheldon:)What sight is better than your little boy
embarrassing a Nobel Iaureate?

